      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Save PMTiles Map Tile\n\nWrites each render into a **PMTiles v3** archive as WebP tiles at `z/x/y`, and\nrebuilds the coarser pyramid levels (`z-1` … `0`) so a whole session becomes one\nzoomable map.\n\nBrowse it at **http://127.0.0.1:8188/pmtiles/** — it refreshes as renders land.\nWith ComfyUI stopped: `./venv/bin/python tools/serve_pmtiles.py`\n\n### Inputs\n\n- **images** — renders to place. Every image in a batch gets its own cell.\n- **map_name** — writes `output/maps/<name>.pmtiles` plus `<name>.tiles.db`. The\n  `.db` is the source of truth (lossless PNG); the `.pmtiles` is rebuilt from it.\n- **z** — zoom level the render is placed on, i.e. the deepest level of the map.\n- **x**, **y** — tile coordinates at that zoom. Ignored when `coords_mode` is\n  `auto_grid`. Can be wired instead of typed.\n- **placement** — `slice` cuts the render into a tile grid at native pixels\n  (1024² with 256 px tiles → 4×4 tiles, which is exactly one tile at `z-2`).\n  `single_tile` resizes the whole render into one tile. `slice` falls back to\n  resizing, and says so, if the render is not a whole number of tiles.\n- **coords_mode** — `manual` uses `x`/`y`. `auto_grid` ignores them and takes the\n  next free block, scanning in growing squares rather than row-major, so\n  re-queueing grows a compact map with no bookkeeping.\n- **tile_size** — 256 or 512. One tile size per map; the store refuses to mix,\n  because the pyramid assumes it.\n- **webp_quality** — 80 by default, applied only when the archive is written. The\n  store stays lossless, so parent tiles never accumulate re-encode loss no matter\n  how many siblings arrive later. Changing this re-encodes every tile.\n- **pyramid_to_zoom** — build derived levels down to this zoom (`0` = a single\n  world tile holding everything).\n- **y_scheme** — how to read the `y` input: `xyz` (y from the top — Leaflet and\n  PMTiles) or `tms` (y from the bottom). Tiles are always *stored* XYZ.\n- **write_archive** — re-serialize the `.pmtiles` after this save. Turn off for a\n  big map and rebuild once with `tools/pmtiles_map.py --rebuild <map>`.\n- **embed_tile_metadata** — carry the per-tile records inside the archive, so the\n  single file is self-describing. Leaf tiles also get an XMP packet either way.\n- **store_full_prompt** — additionally keep the entire graph per tile in the `.db`.\n- **title**, **tags** — free text, shown in the viewer sidebar.\n\n### Outputs\n\n- **images** — passthrough, so the node can sit mid-chain.\n- **info** — what was placed where, as text.\n\nCaptured per tile: prompt, negative, seed, steps, cfg, sampler, scheduler,\ndenoise, model files, latent size, timestamp, title and tags. Click any tile in\nthe viewer to read them back.\n"
      ]
    }
